        <mxCell id="IU5pmkMqKAOoMHPf9lQJ-2" parent="IU5pmkMqKAOoMHPf9lQJ-1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pWvJNd&quot; style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;mZJni&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;ul class=&quot;XSq4R KI3fJ&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; margin: 12px 0px 16px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pWvJNd&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 14px; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;mZJni&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;yhAwj&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;ZLzG0d ncoeY E8xBUb&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot; aria-level=&quot;3&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pWvJNd&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;mZJni&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;yhAwj&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;ZLzG0d ncoeY E8xBUb&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot; aria-level=&quot;3&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pWvJNd&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;mZJni&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;yhAwj&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;ZLzG0d ncoeY E8xBUb&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot; aria-level=&quot;3&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;📝 Production Distributed Caching Cheat Sheet (Interview Edition)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;yhAwj&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;AdPoic&quot; aria-level=&quot;4&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 24px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;1. System Scaling &amp;amp; High Traffic Architecture (For 1M RPS / 1TB Data)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul class=&quot;XSq4R KI3fJ&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; margin: 12px 0px 16px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;The Sharding Principle:&lt;/span&gt; Instead of one giant database server, data is chopped into chunks (&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Shards&lt;/span&gt;). If you have 1TB of data, you spread it across &lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;125 distinct Master containers&lt;/span&gt;, meaning each instance holds a completely unique ~8GB slice of data in its RAM.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Scaling the Hashing Layer:&lt;/span&gt; A single NGINX instance crashes under millions of requests. To fix this, place a super-fast &lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;AWS Network Load Balancer (NLB)&lt;/span&gt; at the front door to split the traffic evenly across a team of &lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;15 NGINX proxy containers&lt;/span&gt;, which all run the exact same math to route keys identically.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Capacity Watchdogs:&lt;/span&gt; Scale up your shard pool if &lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Memory Utilization&lt;/span&gt; crosses &lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;80%&lt;/span&gt; or if your &lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Cache Eviction Rate&lt;/span&gt; spikes (meaning nodes are full and throwing away good keys). Upgrade individual shard sizes (vCPU) if nodes start choking on raw CPU processing or handling too many concurrent network requests.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;yhAwj&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;AdPoic&quot; aria-level=&quot;4&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 24px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;2. Compute &amp;amp; Network Infrastructure (AWS)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul class=&quot;XSq4R KI3fJ&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; margin: 12px 0px 16px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;ECS Fargate (Serverless Brains):&lt;/span&gt; Runs your containers without making you manage real virtual servers or Linux systems. You give every single task the exact same uniform RAM size (e.g., 16GB) so the cluster stays perfectly balanced.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Private Isolation (Security):&lt;/span&gt; Put your cache shards in a hidden &lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Private Subnet&lt;/span&gt; behind firewalls. Set AWS Security Groups so these memory nodes reject everything &lt;em class=&quot;zhvwWe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;unless&lt;/em&gt; it comes directly from your NGINX proxy layer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Dynamic Tracking (AWS Cloud Map):&lt;/span&gt; When containers crash or reboot, their network IP addresses change. Cloud Map acts like a live phonebook, giving the cluster a steady internal domain name (e.g., &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;KDcb0c&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 14px; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(240, 242, 245);&quot;&gt;node.cache.local&lt;/code&gt;) that tracks live container IPs automatically.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;yhAwj&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;AdPoic&quot; aria-level=&quot;4&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 24px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;3. Memory &amp;amp; Engine Safeguards (Node.js Shard Level)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul class=&quot;XSq4R KI3fJ&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; margin: 12px 0px 16px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;V8 Engine Seatbelts:&lt;/span&gt; Node.js doesn&#39;t natively know it is inside a container and can accidentally hog memory until AWS brutally kills it. Pass a hard runtime flag (&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;KDcb0c&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 14px; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(240, 242, 245);&quot;&gt;NODE_OPTIONS=&quot;--max-old-space-size=12288&quot;&lt;/code&gt; for a 16GB task) to force cleanup before a crash happens.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;LRU Eviction Framework:&lt;/span&gt; Never use a raw JavaScript object array forever. Use an &lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;LRU (Least Recently Used) cache library&lt;/span&gt; inside your shard code; when memory hits its ceiling, the shard automatically kicks out the oldest, coldest keys to make room for new ones.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;yhAwj&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;AdPoic&quot; aria-level=&quot;4&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 24px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;4. Traffic Routing &amp;amp; Ring Optimization (NGINX)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul class=&quot;XSq4R KI3fJ&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; margin: 12px 0px 16px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Consistent Hashing Math:&lt;/span&gt; NGINX uses the directive &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;KDcb0c&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 14px; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(240, 242, 245);&quot;&gt;hash $request_uri consistent;&lt;/code&gt; to build a mathematical &lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Ketama Hash Ring&lt;/span&gt;. If one memory node dies, the whole system doesn&#39;t reset; only a tiny fraction of keys are lost, saving your database from a traffic flood.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Virtual Nodes (vnodes):&lt;/span&gt; To avoid &quot;hotspots&quot; where random luck overloads one server while others sit empty, NGINX plots &lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;160 fake/virtual clones&lt;/span&gt; of each server onto the math ring to interleave and perfectly balance the workload.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;TCP Warmth &amp;amp; Recovery:&lt;/span&gt; Add &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;KDcb0c&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 14px; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(240, 242, 245);&quot;&gt;keepalive 32;&lt;/code&gt; to leave network pipelines permanently open, cutting out heavy setup lag. Use &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;KDcb0c&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 14px; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(240, 242, 245);&quot;&gt;max_fails=3 fail_timeout=10s;&lt;/code&gt; so if a node goes down, NGINX instantly skips it and routes requests clockwise to the next healthy instance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;yhAwj&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;AdPoic&quot; aria-level=&quot;4&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 24px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;5. Hot Key Mitigation &amp;amp; Dynamic Salting (App Server Layer)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul class=&quot;XSq4R KI3fJ&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; margin: 12px 0px 16px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Real-Time Radar:&lt;/span&gt; Keep a tiny &lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Sliding Window Counter&lt;/span&gt; in your main app servers. If a specific key (like a viral post) faces a massive traffic surge (&amp;gt;5,000 requests per second), the app instantly flags it as a &lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Hot Key&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Scatter and Read (Salting):&lt;/span&gt; To stop a Hot Key from breaking a single shard, the app server appends a random number to it (e.g., changing &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;KDcb0c&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 14px; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(240, 242, 245);&quot;&gt;viral_post&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;KDcb0c&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 14px; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(240, 242, 245);&quot;&gt;viral_post_3&lt;/code&gt;). NGINX hashes this string and sends it to a completely different node, spreading the viral traffic across multiple servers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Broadcast on Write:&lt;/span&gt; When updating a recognized Hot Key, the app server acts as a copy machine—it writes the update to &lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;all salted variations&lt;/span&gt; (e.g., saving &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;KDcb0c&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 14px; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(240, 242, 245);&quot;&gt;post_1&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;KDcb0c&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 14px; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(240, 242, 245);&quot;&gt;post_2&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;KDcb0c&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 14px; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(240, 242, 245);&quot;&gt;post_3&lt;/code&gt;) through NGINX so every target shard has a copy ready.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;yhAwj&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;AdPoic&quot; aria-level=&quot;4&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 24px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;6. System Resiliency Patterns&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul class=&quot;XSq4R KI3fJ&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; margin: 12px 0px 16px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Cache Stampede Protection:&lt;/span&gt; If a highly popular key expires, you don&#39;t want 10,000 users hitting your primary database at the exact same millisecond. Use a &lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Single-Flight/Mutex lock&lt;/span&gt; on your app server so only the &lt;em class=&quot;zhvwWe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;first&lt;/em&gt; request queries the database to refresh the cache, forcing the other 9,999 to wait cleanly.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;Read/Write Split (Replication):&lt;/span&gt; Double your infrastructure by creating &lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;125 Read Replicas&lt;/span&gt; mapped 1:1 to your Masters. Configure NGINX to route all data changes (&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;KDcb0c&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 14px; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(240, 242, 245);&quot;&gt;POST&lt;/code&gt;) to the Masters—which sync data down asynchronously—while routing all lookup reads (&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;KDcb0c&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 14px; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(240, 242, 245);&quot;&gt;GET&lt;/code&gt;) directly to the Read Replicas.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;yhAwj&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;AHmQrc&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;n6owBd awi2gc&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; margin: 12px 0px 16px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;just one note&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1) have look for lld for designing cache via doubly linked list and hash map .&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;yhAwj&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;yhAwj&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;yhAwj&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;yhAwj&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;SGF5Lb&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;SGF5Lb&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;SGF5Lb&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot; style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1410" width="1050" y="-10" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="IU5pmkMqKAOoMHPf9lQJ-4" edge="1" parent="1" source="dT_7ktCxs0KbFV-aIeWu-24" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.002;entryY=0.479;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;entryPerimeter=0;" target="IU5pmkMqKAOoMHPf9lQJ-3" value="">
          <mxGeometry height="50" relative="1" width="50" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="595" y="255" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="841" y="256" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="IU5pmkMqKAOoMHPf9lQJ-3" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;roundedPerimeter=1;" value="1) have responsibility of storing consistent hash ring&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;2)&amp;nbsp; will have read and write replicas infomation in config file to navigate to awhich replica during which request&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="180" width="245" x="660" y="167.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="IU5pmkMqKAOoMHPf9lQJ-5" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;NGNIX cluster&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
